      339.0713806152344
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "This article presents a brief introduction to the North Munda (Austro-Asiatic) ",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 7.9571852684021,
    "bbox": [
      123.7489013671875,
      331.5113830566406,
      370.1136169433594,
      341.3433837890625
    ],
    "origin": [
      123.7489013671875,
      339.0713806152344
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "language Turi, spoken by some 1,500 speakers throughout the Indian states of Chhat-",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 8.0,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      341.5113830566406,
      368.5138854980469,
      351.3433837890625
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      349.0713806152344
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "tisgarh, Jharkhand, Odisha, Bihar, West Bengal and Assam. After a brief introduction to ",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 8.0,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      351.5113830566406,
      370.1300964355469,
      361.3433837890625
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      359.0713806152344
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "the ethnic Turi group, we present a skeleton grammar of the Turi language as spoken in ",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 8.0,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      361.5113830566406,
      370.1442565917969,
      371.3433837890625
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      369.0713806152344
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "northwestern Odisha state, where it is still being learned by children as their home lan-",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 8.0,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      371.5113830566406,
      368.4636535644531,
      381.3433837890625
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      379.0713806152344
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "guage. We then discuss the position of Turi within the Kherwarian (North Munda) group ",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 8.0,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      381.5113830566406,
      370.0740051269531,
      391.3433837890625
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      389.0713806152344
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "by comparing our lexical data for Turi with that for twelve other Kherwarian varieties as ",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 8.0,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      391.5113830566406,
      370.1227722167969,
      401.3433837890625
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      399.0713806152344
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "given in Kobayashi et al. (2003), using the software COG from the Summer Institute of ",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 8.0,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      401.5113830566406,
      370.08355712890625,
      411.3433837890625
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      409.0713806152344
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "Linguistics. Our results suggest that Turi is a sister language to all of the dialects of Santali ",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 7.9358930587768555,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      411.51141357421875,
      370.0346374511719,
      421.3434143066406
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      419.0714111328125
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "and that it together with these forms the Santali-Turi branch of Kherwarian. We end with ",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 7.989743232727051,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      421.51141357421875,
      370.11083984375,
      431.3434143066406
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      429.0714111328125
    ]
  },
  {
    "text": "a discussion of the possible consequences of these results for the linguistic and ethnic ",
    "font": "SourceSansPro-Light",
    "size": 8.0,
    "bbox": [
      85.0385971069336,
      431.51141357421875,
      370.0979309082031,
      441.3434143066406
    ],
    "origin": [
      85.0385971069336,
      439.0714111328125
